  "result": "I wrote the revised record to `record.jsonl`. The only real change is the `blind` scenario, and it hasn't been through the gate yet.\n\n**Why `blind` failed:** masking only `rel.bearing` can't make the rule unknown. The source just stops supplying a measured bearing, and Core then computes it from the two positions and the subject's heading. Any track whose occupancy is observed must have those fields, and the rule needs both vehicles' occupancy. So the scene still came out violated.\n\n**What I changed:** `blind` now masks `[\"rel.occupies\", \"rel.bearing\"]`, which is the fix the coder suggested. Its narrative now describes this setup:\n- The scene uses the `forbid` geometry: an oncoming car alongside on the subject's right.\n- The source declares `rel.occupies` absent, so whether the two cars are on the same highway is unobserved and the duty is unknown.\n- With occupancy masked, a track no longer needs a heading. That also lets the coder build the variant where the heading is missing, so the bearing can't be computed and both masked atoms drive the unknown.\n\n**Unchanged:** the atom mappings, applicability, obligation, parameters, narrowings and the other scenarios are the same, so the coder's rule should need no change. I also added the definition's and contracts' wording to the two justifications.",
